  "description": "A typesafe F# DSL for building and reading Excel workbooks (.xlsx/.xlsm), interpreted into calls against the DocumentFormat.OpenXml SDK. Unlike write-only Excel generators, this round-trips and can decompile an existing file into equivalent, runnable F# source (Workbook.generateScript) or plain XML against a real embedded schema (Xml.ofWorkbook/Xml.toWorkbook, Xml.xsd) - read a real spreadsheet, get back the code or data that rebuilds it. The XML direction doubles as a way to build an .xlsx from XML a transform engine (e.g. XSLT) already produces, and to convert an existing .xlsx to XML for text-based diffing/version control, with deterministically ordered output so real content changes stay isolated in the diff. Covers cells, styles, formulas (including shared-formula reconstruction on read), conditional formatting, data validation, tables, charts, images, pivot tables (with real aggregation), sparklines, and VBA macro embedding.",
  "id": "Kookerella.FsOpenXmlDsl",
